<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>6.2.3: Multiplying a Polynomial by a Polynomial</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01595</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.2.3: Multiplying a Polynomial by a Polynomial</md:title>
    <md:uuid>566aed3a-50bb-4130-85a2-4c4eb84484b1</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>For questions 1 - 5, match each polynomial expression to its simplified solution. Be prepared to explain or show your work.</para>
<!-- BEGIN ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Activity</title><exercise id="_99fecd6c-c3ad-440d-b80f-2c9a69d3347f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((c+1)(c^2+3c+6)\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(c^3+4c^2+9c+6\).</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is \(c^3+4c^2+9c+6\).</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_7bbd5af4-51cd-455d-bfb0-e04c0e8a09ba" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((c-6)(c^2+c+1) \)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(c^3-5c^2-5c-6\).</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is \(c^3-5c^2-5c-6\).</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="df45d4b3-d0a6-4846-a345-016c629d5648" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((c+5)(c^2+2c-4)\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(c^3+7c^2+6c-20\).</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is \(c^3+7c^2+6c-20\) .</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_5d853b17-d067-438b-a037-032f6c8202b1" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((c^2-3)(c^2-4c-1)\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(c^4-4c^3−4c^2+12c+3 \).</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is \(c^4-4c^3−4c^2+12c+3 \).</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_45acc9f0-2233-4fa7-87d7-3c233b5c49f3" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((c^2+10)(c^2-5c+2)\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(c^4-5c^3+8c^2-50c+20\).</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is \(c^4-5c^3+8c^2-50c+20\).</para></solution></exercise></section><!--END ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->

<!-- BEGIN CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->

<!--Q#6-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Now, fill in the missing blanks to complete the polynomial multiplication.
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}\left(2x-4\right)\left(x^2+\square x-5\right)&amp;=&amp;2x\left(x^2+6x-5\right)-4\left(x^2+6x-\square\right)\\&amp;=&amp;2x^3+\square x^2-10x-4x^2-24x+\square\\&amp;=&amp;\square x^3+8x^2-\square x+20\end{array}\)
    </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}\left(2x-4\right)\left(x^2+6x-5\right)&amp;=&amp;2x\left(x^2+6x-5\right)-4\left(x^2+6x-5\right)\\&amp;=&amp;2x^3+12x^2-10x-4x^2-24x+20\\&amp;=&amp;2x^3+8x^2-34x+20\end{array}\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
<!-- END CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->
<section><title>Video: Multiplying Polynomials Using Different Methods</title>
<para>Watch the following video to learn more about how to multiply polynomials using both the Distributive Property and Vertical Alignment.</para>
<media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text"><iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/60f331c1efb175db53ec991f134d76cf815be109"/></media></section>


<note class="self-check"><para>Multiply.</para>
  <para>\((d+4)(2d^2-3d+5)\)</para></note>


  <section><title>Additional Resources</title>
    <section><title>Multiplying a Polynomial by a Polynomial</title>
      <para>We have multiplied monomials by monomials, monomials by polynomials, and binomials by binomials. Now we’re ready to multiply a polynomial by a polynomial. Remember, FOIL will not work in this case, but we can use other representations of the Distributive Property such as Vertical Alignment or distributing individual terms or polynomials.</para>
      
      <para><emphasis>Example 1</emphasis></para>
      <para>Multiply \((b+3)(2b^2-5b+8)\) using the Distributive Property by distributing either a binomial or an individual term.</para>
      
      <para><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> 
        Distribute. \({\style{color:red}(}
        {\style{color:red}2}
        {\style{color:red}b}
        ^
        {\style{color:red}2} \;{\style{color:red}-}\;     {\style{color:red}5}
        {\style{color:red}b}\;     {\style{color:red}+} \;{\style{color:red}8}
        {\style{color:red})}\).
        \(b
        {\style{color:red}(}
        {\style{color:red}2}
        {\style{color:red}b}
        ^
        {\style{color:red}2}\;     {\style{color:red}-}\;     {\style{color:red}5}
        {\style{color:red}b}\;     {\style{color:red}+}\;     {\style{color:red}8}
        {\style{color:red})}
        +3
        {\style{color:red}(}
        {\style{color:red}2}
        {\style{color:red}b}
        ^
        {\style{color:red}2} \;{\style{color:red}-}\;     {\style{color:red}5}
        {\style{color:red}b} \;{\style{color:red}+}\;     {\style{color:red}8}
        {\style{color:red})}
        \)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> 
        Multiply.
        \(2b^3-5b^2+8b+6b^2-15b+24\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> 
        Combine like terms.
        \(2b^3+b^2-7b+24\)</para>
      
      <para><emphasis>Example 2</emphasis></para>
      <para>Multiply \((b+3)(2b^2-5b+8)\) using vertical alignment.</para>
      
      <para>It is easier to put the polynomial with fewer terms on the bottom because we get fewer partial products this way.</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> 
        Multiply. \((2b^2-5b+8)\) by \(3\).</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> 
        Multiply. \((2b^2-5b+8)\) by \(b\).</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> 
        Add like terms.</para>
      <para>\(\underline{\underline{\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;2b^2-\;5b+8\\\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\times\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;b+3}\\ \; \\\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;6b^2-15b+24\\2b^3-5b^2\;+8b}\\ \; \\ 2b^3 \; +\;b^2-\;7b+24\)</para>
      
      <note class="try">
      <title>Try It: Multiplying a Polynomial by a Polynomial</title>
      
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          
          <para>For questions 1 - 2, Multiply \((z-3)(z^2-5z+2)\) using the listed method.</para>
          
          <para>The Distributive Property</para>
          <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        
        </problem><solution>
        <para>Compare your answer: You answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
          
          <para><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> Distribute. \((z^2 - 5z + 2)\).
            \(z(z^2-5z+2)-3(z^2-5z+2)\)</para>
          
          <para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> 
            Multiply.
            \(z^3-5z^2+2z-3z^2+15z-6\)</para>
          
          <para><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> 
            Combine like terms.
            \(z^3-8z^2+17z-6\)</para>
      
      </solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise>
        <problem>
       
          
          <para>Vertical Alignment</para>
          <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        
        </problem><solution>
        <para>Compare your answer: You answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
          
          
          
          <para><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> 
            Multiply. \((z^2-5z+2)\) by \(–3\).</para>
          
          <para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> 
            Multiply.  \((z^2-5z+2)\) by \(z\).</para>
          
          <para><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> 
            Add like terms.</para>
          
          <para>\(\underline{\underline{\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;z^2-5z+2\\\;\;\;\;\times\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;z-3}\\ \;\; \\ \;\;\;\;-3z^2+15z-6\\\;z^3-5z^2+2z}\\ \;\; \\z^3-8z^2+17z-6\)</para>
      
      </solution></exercise></note>
      </section>
  </section>
